8480000.0,"attribution":"www.absolutegeeks.com"}]},{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"www.theverge.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://www.theverge.com/tech/961332/qi-active-cooling-really-works","title":"Qi fan fan","snippet":"The author endorses wireless Qi chargers with integrated fans after testing Kuxiu\u2019s $59.99 D5 Qi2.2 charging dock for a week. Active cooling kept the phone noticeably cooler than conventional wireless chargers, addressing concerns about lithium-ion battery degradation and charging slowdowns caused by heat. The author\u2019s concern is personal: an iPhone 15 Pro previously suffered a failed logic board while performing demanding tasks and charging in hot conditions, resulting in a repair costing more than $750, though covered by warranty. The D5 includes a quiet, optional fan, strong magnetic alignment, a useful power-and-time display, and a 45W USB-C charger. It can deliver up to 25W to compatible phones, plus power for watches and earbuds. However, its \u201c5-in-1\u201d label is misleading because only three devices charge simultaneously; the animated display is distracting, and the motorized watch charger feels over-engineered. Overall, the dock is considered a good, relatively affordable desktop or bedside option. The author argues active cooling will become increasingly important as wireless charging speeds rise toward a planned global 50W Qi standard by 2028.","ref_id":{"turn_index":701695,"ref_type":"news","ref_index":12},"pub_date":1783148400.0,"thumbnail_url":"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/HQ6ok0NPHkLhv03OhDEy9s8Z_9cf2eg-LFJ4krqT13yUUnTjsPq2_cMsOnABv8MNrErzDBgqPLt9OpTJuWsbjkkXtKXaPn6cUTq9Wo0LHZjl9iz2_OEaIvs6gUIw3bqOK5xy8rQGlpbgXigYss8OqRYYN4KdGWcn_BY3nXuHzEuskoWsyRjGAICpr0UhsloWPIlj-INZr--EipKH9WX6v5ijteuQp1HDmSAHYz8iF8Hz26xmbtk-mIO2nGzOYFB5","attribution":"www.theverge.com"}]},{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"mobileplustech.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://mobileplus